{"name":"Evening Dress","hex":"#d1a19b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"evening dress","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An elegant dress worn by women, especially for social events in the evening, an evening gown.","Formal attire worn for evening social events."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evening_dress"}],"entries":[{"title":"Evening gown","blocks":[{"text":"An evening gown, evening dress or gown is a long dress usually worn at formal occasions. The drop ranges from ballerina, tea, to full-length. Such gowns are typically worn with evening gloves. Evening gowns are usually made of luxurious fabrics such as chiffon, velvet, satin, or organza. Silk is a popular fibre for many evening gowns. Although the terms are used interchangeably, ball gowns and evening gowns differ in that a ball gown will always have a full skirt and a fitted bodice, while an evening gown can be any silhouette—sheath, mermaid, fit and flare, A-line, or trumpet-shaped—and may have straps, halters or even sleeves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Evening_gown.jpg/330px-Evening_gown.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evening_gown"},{"title":"White tie","blocks":[{"text":"White tie, also called full evening dress or a dress suit, is the most formal evening Western dress code. For men, it consists of a black tail coat worn over a white dress shirt with a starched or piqué bib, white piqué waistcoat and the white bow tie worn around a standing wing collar. Mid or high-waisted black trousers with galon, a braid of trim consisting of two silk stripes to conceal the outer seams of the trousers, along with court shoes complete the outfit. Orders, decorations and medals in miniature may be worn. Acceptable accessories include a black top hat, white gloves, a white scarf, a pocket watch, a white pocket square, and a boutonnière. Women wear full-length ball or evening gowns with evening gloves and, optionally, tiaras, jewellery, and a small handbag."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Dolores_del_R%C3%ADo_%26Fred_Astaire_in_Flying_Down_to_Rio.jpg/330px-Dolores_del_R%C3%ADo_%26Fred_Astaire_in_Flying_Down_to_Rio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_tie"},{"title":"Evening Dress (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Evening Dress is a 1986 French comedy-drama film directed by Bertrand Blier. It was entered into the 1986 Cannes Film Festival where Michel Blanc won the award for Best Actor."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/de/Tenue_de_soir%C3%A9e.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evening_Dress_(film)"},{"title":"Evening","blocks":[{"text":"Evening is the period of a day that begins at the end of afternoon and overlaps with the beginning of night. It starts when the sun is close to the horizon and, according to most definitions, spans the period of night before bedtime or midnight. The exact times when evening begins and ends are subjective and depend on location and time of year. In some cases, evening is considered to begin during daylight; before sunset."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Evening_in_Parambikkulam%2C_Kerala%2C_India.jpg/330px-Evening_in_Parambikkulam%2C_Kerala%2C_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evening"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Maria_Grazia_Cucinotta_-_nicogenin_-_66%C3%A8me_Festival_de_Venise_%28Mostra%29_2.jpg/500px-Maria_Grazia_Cucinotta_-_nicogenin_-_66%C3%A8me_Festival_de_Venise_%28Mostra%29_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Maria_Grazia_Cucinotta_-_nicogenin_-_66%C3%A8me_Festival_de_Venise_%28Mostra%29_2.jpg/500px-Maria_Grazia_Cucinotta_-_nicogenin_-_66%C3%A8me_Festival_de_Venise_%28Mostra%29_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Maria Grazia Cucinotta wearing a black evening gown at the Venice Film Festival","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaria_Grazia_Cucinotta_-_nicogenin_-_66%C3%A8me_Festival_de_Venise_(Mostra)_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Wedding_Supper_-_Martin_van_Meytens_-_Google_Cultural_Institute.jpg/500px-Wedding_Supper_-_Martin_van_Meytens_-_Google_Cultural_Institute.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Wedding_Supper_-_Martin_van_Meytens_-_Google_Cultural_Institute.jpg/1280px-Wedding_Supper_-_Martin_van_Meytens_-_Google_Cultural_Institute.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Wedding_Supper_-_Martin_van_Meytens_-_Google_Cultural_Institute.jpg/500px-Wedding_Supper_-_Martin_van_Meytens_-_Google_Cultural_Institute.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wedding supper of Princess Isabella of Parma and future Holy Roman Emperor Joseph II, 1760; female attendees are shown wearing ornate court gowns decorated with lace and jewels","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWedding_Supper_-_Martin_van_Meytens_-_Google_Cultural_Institute.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Evening_gowns%2C_1947.jpg/500px-Evening_gowns%2C_1947.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Evening_gowns%2C_1947.jpg/1280px-Evening_gowns%2C_1947.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conten